      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Next time you see this happening, note if your framerate is far below 45fps or not.\n\nAudio crackling usually happens when your frame rate is lower than that of the video being played to play the music.\n\nIf you are staying at or above 45 easily, and the audio is still crackling, then it seems like the video being played for the music may be a 60fps video. And in that case,​ you would need perfect framerate above 60fps to play that nicely.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
